From 872a50f5a3c1f78f06951d2a5be211deaa08a74d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:19:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] ipq40xx: base-files: start a login only on the console

The target's inittab starts a login prompt on ttyMSM1 as well as on
ttyMSM0, whatever ttyMSM1 is wired to. On the Arista W-118 it is the
UART of the Bluetooth LE controller: the login took the controller's
HCI replies, so btattach's HCI Reset timed out, and it wrote its
"Please press Enter" prompt into the controller.

Drop the target's inittab for the default one, whose askconsole runs
the login on the kernel console, wherever console= points.

/etc/inittab is a conffile, so systems upgraded with their settings
kept keep the old one.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/inittab | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/inittab

diff --git a/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/inittab b/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/inittab
deleted file mode 100644
index 3181021a..00000000
--- a/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/inittab
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,5 +0,0 @@
-# Copyright (c) 2013 The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.
-::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS S boot
-::shutdown:/etc/init.d/rcS K shutdown
-ttyMSM0::askfirst:/usr/libexec/login.sh
-ttyMSM1::askfirst:/usr/libexec/login.sh
